<section class="case-section contribution-block" aria-labelledby="kitty-contributions">
    <h2 id="kitty-contributions">My Contributions</h2>
    <p>As <strong>Producer / Programmer</strong>, I coordinated a seven-person team through release and a seasonal update. My primary responsibilities were production, scope management, and team communication, supported by hands-on testing and bug fixes.</p>
    <ul>
        <li>Coordinated work across multiple mini-games and the shared game structure.</li>
        <li>Delegated tasks and followed progress through team meetings.</li>
        <li>Helped balance feature scope against team bandwidth and release priorities.</li>
        <li>Supported presentations and communication of the project’s progress.</li>
        <li>Combined production responsibilities with testing and programming support.</li>
    </ul>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-about">
    <h2 id="kitty-about">About This Game</h2>

    <p>Kitty Casino is a mobile casual casino game built around five mini-games, a casino hub, Story Mode unlocks, and cat cosmetics. Our seven-person team took it from concept to release and followed it with a Christmas-themed content update.</p>


    <figure><img src={`${base}KittyCasinoMedia1.png`} alt="Kitty Casino gameplay interface" loading="lazy" /></figure>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-production">
    <h2 id="kitty-production">Production &amp; Team Coordination</h2>
    <p>The central production challenge was keeping several parallel gameplay features moving toward one shipped product. Each mini-game needed its own development attention, but the team also had to deliver the hub, progression, cosmetics, and the transitions that connected them.</p>
    <h3>Coordinating a seven-person team</h3>
    <p>I organized meetings, delegated tasks, and tracked progress across the mini-games and shared systems. These check-ins helped identify work that needed support; presentations communicated the game’s progress and kept the team aligned.</p>

    <h3>Managing scope through integration</h3>
    <p>I helped weigh feature scope against team capacity and release priorities. Each mini-game needed to fit the unlock flow and shared interface, so integration and cross-feature testing remained part of the work rather than waiting until every feature was finished.</p>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-scope">
    <h2 id="kitty-scope">Managing Multi-Game Scope</h2>
    <div class="tags" aria-label="Kitty Casino mini-games">{["Blackjack", "Poker", "Slots", "Matching", "Bartending"].map(game => <span>{game}</span>)}</div>
    <p>The five mini-games brought different rules and interactions into the same product. Bartending also provided a way back into play when the player ran out of money, tying it to the broader game flow.</p>
    <p>I tracked these parallel features alongside their shared integration work, keeping a connected, release-ready casino experience as the target.</p>
    <figure><img src={`${base}KittyCasinoMedia5.png`} alt="One of Kitty Casino’s mini-game interfaces" loading="lazy" /></figure>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-progression">
    <h2 id="kitty-progression">Progression &amp; Game Structure</h2>
    <p>The casino hub connects the mini-games, while Story Mode provides an unlock flow that gives players a reason to move between them. The cosmetics shop adds another use for winnings, letting players purchase accessories and personalize their cat.</p>
    <p>I supported this overall structure through production, scope coordination, and testing. The team’s progression and cosmetics work had to fit around the individual mini-games and give the combined experience a clear flow.</p>
    <figure><img src={`${base}KittyCasinoMedia3.png`} alt="Kitty Casino progression and customization interface" loading="lazy" /></figure>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-dlc">
    <h2 id="kitty-dlc">Post-Launch / Christmas DLC</h2>
    <p>After the original release, I coordinated a Christmas-themed update that reskinned the casino and mini-games with festive assets. This extended the production work into post-launch support, with new scope spread across several existing game areas.</p>
    <p>I helped manage the added scope and coordinate themed changes across the hub and mini-games while preserving the existing progression flow.</p>
    <figure><img src={`${base}KittyCasinoMedia7.png`} alt="Kitty Casino Christmas-themed update" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The Christmas update brought themed content to the existing game after release.</figcaption></figure>
</section>
<section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="kitty-qa">
    <h2 id="kitty-qa">QA &amp; Release Support</h2>
    <p>I supported cross-feature testing, issue reporting, and bug fixes. After changes, I revisited mini-game transitions, Story Mode unlocks, and cosmetics to check for regressions and help prepare the integrated game for release.</p>
</section>
